<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (1. NumPy arrays are faster than Python lists \(implemented in C, not pure Python\). 2. They store elements in contiguous memory \(better cache performance\). 3. They are also homogenous i.e. all elements have same type. 4. They use vectorized operations \(no slow Python loops\). )
/E (1. NumPy arrays are faster than Python lists \(implemented in C, not pure Python\). 2. They store elements in contiguous memory \(better cache performance\). 3. They are also homogenous i.e. all elements have same type. 4. They use vectorized operations \(no slow Python loops\). )
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
